[[File:Kurask icon.png|left]]
'''Kurask''' are [[Slayer monsters]] that require a [[Slayer]] level of 70 to kill. Like [[turoth]], they can only be damaged with [[leaf-bladed weapons]], [[Broad-tipped ammunition|broad ammunition]], or the [[Magic Dart]] spell due to their tough hides;{{CiteNPC|npc=Slayer Master|quote=Kurask are large brutal creatures with very thick hides. You'll need a Leaf-Tipped Spear, Sword or Battle-axe, Broad Arrows, or a Magic Dart to harm it.|loc=|notes=|name=}} they are immune to any other types of attacks. They are, however, susceptible to [[burn]] damage from weapons such as [[burning claws]].

Kurask are relatively inaccurate, but they can hit somewhat high if their attacks manage to land. Additionally, they have fast health regeneration, healing one [[Hitpoints|hitpoint]] every five [[Game tick|game ticks]]. They can be fought without [[protection prayers]] by using [[Bones to Peaches]] for healing, though players may wish to activate [[Protect from Melee]] if the [[Superior slayer monster|superior version]], the [[king kurask]], spawns.

Although kurask are invulnerable to any damage from the special attacks of [[Saradomin godsword]], [[ancient godsword]], and [[toxic blowpipe]], their healing effects will still activate as if damage had been dealt, making them useful as special attack weapons during extended trips. Likewise, the special attacks of [[ancient mace]] and [[eldritch Nightmare staff]] will restore [[prayer points]] based on what damage would have been dealt. The set effect of [[Guthan the Infested's equipment|Guthan's equipment]] will not activate against kurask, however.

Kurask have a relatively small aggressive range of 2, with the centre at their south-west tile. As they are 3x3 monsters, they will only attack you from their north-east side if they walk under your true tile.  

Kurask drop the [[leaf-bladed sword]]. They are also known for their [[Mystic robe top (light)|light mystic robe top]] and [[kurask head]] drops, as well as being the only monster (including their superior version) to drop the [[leaf-bladed battleaxe]]. 

